[img]IMAGE_BASE/banner.png[/img]

Grow cannabis the way Project Zomboid grows everything else: plow, sow, water and harvest it as a vanilla crop. Then dry it, trim it, cure it and smoke it. Sexed seeds, breeding, clones, grow lights, grow bags and three hydro systems. Built for [b]Build 42[/b], multiplayer ready.

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/changelog/WORKSHOP_ID][img]IMAGE_BASE/b-changes.png[/img][/url] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussions/WORKSHOP_ID][img]IMAGE_BASE/b-discuss.png[/img][/url]

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-whats-in.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Five growth stages[/b] on vanilla farming. Plots, watering, pests and the Sow Seed menu work as usual.
[*][b]Indica, Sativa and Hybrid[/b], with male and female seeds, breeding, and genetics that drift.
[*][b]Clones[/b] of your best plant, with rooting gel and a cloning dome.
[*][b]Grow lamps, flood lights and light timers[/b] for indoor grows.
[*][b]Grow bags, DWC, RDWC and flood tables.[/b]
[*][b]Drying racks, fans, curing jars and barrels.[/b] Buds range from Poor to Top Shelf.
[*][b]Joints and pipes[/b], with tolerance and optional dependency.
[*]How much you can tell about a plant depends on your [b]Agriculture[/b] level.
[*]Gear and seeds turn up as loot. Recipes come from the [i]Grower's Handbook[/i] and [i]Hydroponics Monthly[/i].
[/list]

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-steps.png[/img]
[img]IMAGE_BASE/steps.png[/img]

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-genetics.png[/img]
[img]IMAGE_BASE/strains.png[/img]
By default, [b]1 seed in 10[/b] is male. A male within 6 tiles of a flowering female pollinates her, so she gives seeds as well as buds. Stress a flowering female too hard and she may turn hermie.

[b]Cloning:[/b] take a cutting from a plant in Vegetative or Pre-flower (you'll need scissors or a knife). Rooting gel, a Cloning Dome and a higher Agriculture level all raise the odds. A rooted clone starts in Vegetative and carries its mother's genetics.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-lights.png[/img]
[img]IMAGE_BASE/lights.png[/img]
Indoors, a plant with no light stops growing. Hang a grow lamp or stand a flood light near it; the large and pro models reach further. Fit a [b]Light Timer[/b]: 18/6 keeps plants in veg, 12/12 makes them flower. Light leaking into a 12/12 plant's dark hours stresses it.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-grow.png[/img]
[img]IMAGE_BASE/grow.png[/img]
Hydro plants need a medium (rockwool or clay pebbles), a reservoir with water and nutrients, and power for the pumps. Old or tainted water brings [b]root rot[/b]. Catch it early and bleach cures it. An RDWC control bucket feeds up to 6 sites within 3 tiles. With [b]Dazed Plumbing[/b] installed, reservoirs can take a water line from a tank.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-cure.png[/img]
[img]IMAGE_BASE/quality.png[/img]
Wet plants take [b]2 days[/b] on a drying rack. A fan within 3 tiles speeds that up and cuts the risk of mold. Trim dry plants into buds, then cure them for [b]6 days[/b] in a jar or barrel. Burp the jar every day and a half or mold creeps in.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-smoke.png[/img]
[table]
[tr][th]Strain[/th][th]What it does[/th][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Indica[/b][/td][td]Melts stress and unhappiness. Leaves you sleepy and hungry.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Sativa[/b][/td][td]Kills boredom and wakes you up. Too strong a hit makes you anxious.[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Hybrid[/b][/td][td]A bit of both.[/td][/tr]
[/table]
Better buds hit harder and last longer, and moldy ones make you feel worse. Regular use builds [b]tolerance[/b]. With Dependency on, heavy users go through withdrawal when they stop.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-settings.png[/img]
Everything is tunable in [b]Sandbox Options › CannabisMod[/b]: growth speed, harvest size, male seed chance, drying and curing time, mold, lamp range and power, high strength, tolerance and dependency, loot rarity, whether recipes need the magazine, root rot, reservoir use, the RDWC quality bonus and pump power.

[b]Servers:[/b] add [b]DazedDank[/b] to [b]Mods=[/b] and [b]WORKSHOP_ID[/b] to [b]WorkshopItems=[/b]. The server keeps every plant, so update the server and all clients together.
[b]Tile sheets:[/b] Dazed Dank uses tile IDs [b]7420[/b] and [b]7421[/b]. Another mod using either of those will clash.

[img]IMAGE_BASE/h-help.png[/img]
Send [b]%UserProfile%\Zomboid\console.txt[/b] right after the problem happens, before you restart. Say whether it was single player or a server, and list your other mods. Post it in the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussions/WORKSHOP_ID]Discussions[/url].
